WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.199
"Our new house looks amazing!" a woman said.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.552
Her husband nodded. "I can't wait to go inside."

3
00:00:09.553 --> 00:00:12.961
A big man in overalls and a hard hat stood nearby.

4
00:00:12.962 --> 00:00:17.700
"Go in," he said. "You're going to love it."

5
00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:20.190
The couple went in.

6
00:00:20.191 --> 00:00:27.630
The wife gasped. "Everything is crooked!"

7
00:00:27.631 --> 00:00:32.813
The husband scratched his head. "The builder did a terrible job!"

8
00:00:32.814 --> 00:00:35.928
As he turned to go back outside, the floor opened up.

9
00:00:35.929 --> 00:00:46.121
The couple screamed and tumbled into darkness.

10
00:00:46.122 --> 00:00:52.111
"Ugh! I'm so tired of this dreary rain!" Mara said.

11
00:00:52.112 --> 00:00:54.766
Roxy and her friends were on their way to school.

12
00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:58.631
The sky was filled with gray clouds, and rain was falling lightly.

13
00:00:58.632 --> 00:01:01.063
"Me too," Roxy said.

14
00:01:01.064 --> 00:01:06.043
"It feels like it's been raining for weeks. I miss the sun."

15
00:01:06.044 --> 00:01:10.016
"I like the rain." Jack looked up and held his mouth open.

16
00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:12.703
He caught some raindrops on his tongue.

17
00:01:12.704 --> 00:01:15.044
Terrell wiped raindrops off his glasses.

18
00:01:15.045 --> 00:01:20.959
"Well, I hate when it rains all day long," he said. "It means—"

19
00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:26.399
"Indoor recess!" Mara said with a groan.

20
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.848
"Indoor recess stinks," Jack said.

21
00:01:29.849 --> 00:01:31.481
He stomped in a puddle.

22
00:01:31.482 --> 00:01:36.897
Water splashed everywhere. "It's so boring!"

23
00:01:36.898 --> 00:01:41.962
Rain fell harder now. The friends walked more quickly.

24
00:01:41.963 --> 00:01:45.009
Heavy raindrops drummed against their umbrellas.

25
00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:49.362
"At least it will be quiet in school today," Mara said.

26
00:01:49.363 --> 00:01:53.574
"The construction work is finally done."

27
00:01:53.575 --> 00:01:57.724
Workers had been at school every day for the past three weeks.

28
00:01:57.725 --> 00:02:03.307
Principal Penn had said the building was old and needed some repairs.

29
00:02:03.308 --> 00:02:05.460
Terrell shot a quick look at Roxy.

30
00:02:05.461 --> 00:02:09.050
"I hope Rocket Girl doesn't have to do anything today."

31
00:02:09.051 --> 00:02:11.490
Mara looked over. "Why?"

32
00:02:11.491 --> 00:02:14.206
Terrell shrugged. "It's raining.

33
00:02:14.207 --> 00:02:17.632
It must be hard to fight villains in the rain."

34
00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:20.745
Jack laughed. "No way!

35
00:02:20.746 --> 00:02:22.511
Rocket Girl is super tough.

36
00:02:22.512 --> 00:02:25.018
Rain doesn't bother her."

37
00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:27.791
Roxy shot a quick look at Terrell and smiled.

38
00:02:27.792 --> 00:02:29.329
"I agree with Terrell.

39
00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:34.801
Rocket Girl probably doesn't want to get soaked while fighting villains."

40
00:02:34.802 --> 00:02:39.922
When they reached the school, Roxy's watch beeped.

41
00:02:39.923 --> 00:02:44.300
She sneaked away from her friends and stood close to the building.

42
00:02:44.301 --> 00:02:48.518
"Mayor Bloom," she said. "What's wrong?"

43
00:02:48.519 --> 00:02:51.056
The mayor had a worried look on his face.

44
00:02:51.057 --> 00:02:53.851
"I'm not sure if anything is wrong, Rocket Girl.

45
00:02:53.852 --> 00:02:57.531
But I tried to call Detective Smith, and he didn't answer his phone.

46
00:02:57.532 --> 00:03:00.306
I can't reach any other police officers either.

47
00:03:00.307 --> 00:03:03.303
I'm worried that something happened to them."

48
00:03:03.304 --> 00:03:05.870
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy said.

49
00:03:05.871 --> 00:03:10.744
"I'll find out what's going on."

